{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJust back from the most incredible trip to Japan! It was a whirlwind of ancient traditions and futuristic technology, a truly captivating contrast.\n\nFirst stop: Kyoto. I wandered through serene bamboo forests, marveling at the golden Kinkaku-ji (Golden Pavilion). The geishas gracefully gliding through Gion were a magical sight.  I spent hours exploring Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vibrant red torii gates winding up the mountain.\n\nThen it was off to Tokyo – a sensory overload in the best way possible.  Shibuya Crossing was an experience – a controlled chaos of people!  I explored the quirky shops of Harajuku, devoured delicious ramen, and got lost in the electric atmosphere of Akihabara.  \n\nThe food was, of course, a highlight. From fresh sushi to savory okonomiyaki, every meal was a delight.  I even braved a vending machine for hot corn soup – surprisingly delicious!\n\nBeyond the sights and tastes, it was the kindness and politeness of the Japanese people that truly stood out.  Everyone was so helpful and welcoming, even with the language barrier.\n\nJapan is a country that stays with you. It’s a place where you can feel both completely immersed in a different culture and surprisingly at home.  I can't wait to go back!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.001122916815802455}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.1602802574634552}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.001033129869028926}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.1345929354429245}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.14395365118980408}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.20775321125984192}, {"token": "Just", "logprob": -0.9361631870269775}, {"token": "▁back", "logprob": -0.03592311963438988}, {"token": "▁from